Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:52:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 4657: the name search scans the owner's labels once, not
 twice at once

Box 54290 (the founder's account, 12 Oct 10:14Z): a name search for a
contact who is his own contact and a member timed out twice (8.6 s each),
so the run answered from a namesake on the web. His 1,908 numbers carry
89,308 labels; the search ran its regex scan over them in two parallel
queries, one for the page and one for the total. The total is now read
from the same scan's hits (a scalar over the hits CTE), so the scan runs
once. Read-only timing on live: each label branch alone is a few seconds.
No new text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
